<Base title="About"><header class="page-head"><p class="eyebrow">Why keep the ugly versions?</p><h1>About the archive</h1><p class="lead">They Forgot the Alamo is an unfinished, low-poly browser game about a man who believes he’s Davy Crockett. This site records how it became itself.</p></header><section class="section"><h2>What you’re seeing</h2><p>The playable build is currently a single room for movement, aiming, destruction, PS1-flavored rendering, and a raccoon perspective swap. It is an experiment with a wonderfully unreasonable premise, not a finished campaign.</p><p>Entries are reconstructed from surviving Git commits, task records, screenshots, model renders, and the game source. Dates are assigned from evidence, not made up to fill a calendar. Later screenshots used to illustrate older versions are identified as such.</p></section><section class="section"><h2>Archive policy</h2><p>Old assets, failed ideas, bugs, and provisional poses belong here. The first surviving game commit is September 29, 2026. That is the oldest confirmed project date in this repository, not a claim about when someone first had the idea.</p></section></Base>
